# **M-Prod sub-track #9 (chaos + fuzz).** libFuzzer runtime state
# is regenerated on every `cargo fuzz run` invocation; only the
# manifest + targets + the *seed* corpus (`fuzz/corpus/<target>/*`
# checked-in seed exemplars) live in version control.
#
# Per-target corpora that libFuzzer grows during the run land in
# `corpus/<target>/` next to the seeds; we ignore everything under
# `corpus/` to keep the slice minimal. The seed corpus directory
# (and its readme) is force-included via `!` rules below.

# Build outputs (cargo + libFuzzer).
target/
Cargo.lock

# Crash + leak + slow-input artifacts surfaced by libFuzzer. The
# CI lane (.github/workflows/ci.yml :: fuzz) uploads this directory
# on failure via `actions/upload-artifact@v4 if: failure()`.
artifacts/

# Coverage / instrumentation runs.
coverage/

# Discovered corpus inputs (libFuzzer mutator output). Kept out of
# version control to avoid the corpus directory drifting silently
# on every developer's machine; the canonical seeds live under
# `corpus/<target>/seeds/` and are re-included by the `!` rules.
corpus/*

# Re-include the per-target *seed* corpora. These are the
# hand-written + format-canonical JSON exemplars that bootstrap a
# 10-min CI fuzz run from cold; without them the run finds shallow
# bugs only.
!corpus/fuzz_management_api_bodies/
corpus/fuzz_management_api_bodies/*
!corpus/fuzz_management_api_bodies/seed_*
